<p>Brick-and-mortar businesses win when they are physically close to the searcher. A pizza shop three blocks away outranks a better pizza shop ten miles away. For contractors, proximity still matters, but it is not the deciding factor. Google knows a plumber can drive 20 miles. What matters more is whether Google trusts that plumber to do good work.</p>
<p>That trust comes from three pillars: <strong>relevance</strong> (does your profile match the search?), <strong>prominence</strong> (are you well-known and well-reviewed online?), and <strong>proximity</strong> (are you reasonably close to the searcher?). For service-area businesses, prominence and relevance carry far more weight than they do for storefronts.</p>
