<h3>Service Area Configuration</h3>
<p>Service areas tell Google where you are willing to travel. They also tell homeowners whether you serve their neighborhood.</p>
<p><strong>How to configure service areas:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Start with your home base city</strong> — This is where you have the strongest proximity signal.</li>
<li><strong>Add adjacent cities</strong> — List cities in order of importance to your business.</li>
<li><strong>Include ZIP codes for precision</strong> — For large metro areas, ZIP codes give Google more granular data than city names alone.</li>
<li><strong>Update seasonally</strong> — If you expand into a new market or stop serving a distant area, update your service areas immediately.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Common mistake:</strong> Listing 20 random cities across a 200-mile radius. Google sees this as spam. Be realistic about where you actually send technicians.</p>
<h3>Business Description Optimization</h3>
<p>Your GBP business description has a 750-character limit. Every character should work.</p>
<p><strong>Formula for a high-converting description:</strong></p>
<div class="code-block">
<pre><code>[Business name] is a [trade] serving [primary city] and [surrounding areas]. 
We specialize in [top 2-3 services] with [key differentiator: 24/7 availability, 
20+ years experience, licensed and insured, etc.]. [Social proof: 500+ 5-star reviews, 
BBB A+ rated]. Call [phone number] for [primary CTA: free estimate, emergency service, etc.].
</code></pre>
</div>
<p><strong>Example for a plumber:</strong></p>
<blockquote class="highlight-quote">
<p>"ClearFlow Plumbing is a licensed plumber serving Dallas, Plano, Richardson, and Frisco. We specialize in emergency plumbing repair, drain cleaning, and water heater installation with 24/7 availability and same-day service. With over 500 five-star Google reviews and a BBB A+ rating, we are the trusted choice for homeowners across North Texas. Call (214) 555-0199 for a free estimate."</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>What to include:</strong><br />
- Your primary service keyword naturally<br />
- Your primary city and 2-3 surrounding cities<br />
- Your top services<br />
- A credibility signal (reviews, years in business, licensing)<br />
- A phone number (clickable on mobile)<br />
- A clear call to action</p>
<p><strong>What to avoid:</strong><br />
- Keyword stuffing<br />
- All caps<br />
- Promotional language ("best," "cheapest")<br />
- URLs (they are not clickable in the description)<br />
- Special characters or emojis</p>
