<h3>Post Strategy</h3>
<p>Google Posts are free mini-ads that appear on your GBP. They expire after seven days, which means you should post weekly to maintain visibility.</p>
<p><strong>Post types that work for contractors:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>What's New</strong> — Share a recent project completion with before/after photos.</li>
<li><strong>Offers</strong> — Promote seasonal discounts ("$50 off AC tune-ups this month").</li>
<li><strong>Events</strong> — Announce free homeowner workshops or community events.</li>
<li><strong>Products</strong> — Highlight specific services with pricing.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Post formula:</strong><br />
- <strong>Headline:</strong> 4-5 words with a benefit ("New Roof Installation in Frisco")<br />
- <strong>Body:</strong> 1-2 sentences describing the project or offer<br />
- <strong>Call to action button:</strong> "Call now," "Book online," or "Learn more"<br />
- <strong>Photo:</strong> High-quality image related to the post</p>
<p><strong>Posting schedule:</strong> One post per week minimum. The businesses that post weekly see 70% more engagement than those that post monthly or less, according to Google.</p>
<h3>Q&amp;A Optimization</h3>
<p>The Q&amp;A section on your GBP is one of the most underutilized ranking factors. It is also a prime opportunity to place location and service keywords naturally.</p>
<p><strong>How to optimize Q&amp;A:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Seed the first 10 questions yourself.</strong> Log out of your Google account (or use a different Google account) and ask common questions. Then answer them from your business account.</li>
<li><strong>Include keywords in questions and answers.</strong> For example:</li>
<li>Q: "Do you offer emergency plumbing service in Plano?"</li>
<li>A: "Yes, we provide 24/7 emergency plumbing repair throughout Plano, Frisco, and McKinney. Our technicians typically arrive within 60 minutes. Call (214) 555-0199 anytime."</li>
<li><strong>Monitor and answer new questions within 24 hours.</strong> Google sends notifications when someone asks a question on your profile.</li>
<li><strong>Upvote your own seeded questions.</strong> Questions with more upvotes appear first.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>10 seeded questions every contractor should add:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Do you offer [primary service] in [city]? — Include your top city.</li>
<li>What areas do you serve? — List all service areas.</li>
<li>Are you licensed and insured? — State your credentials.</li>
<li>Do you offer free estimates? — Clarify your pricing approach.</li>
<li>What are your business hours? — Include emergency availability.</li>
<li>How quickly can you respond to emergencies? — Set expectations.</li>
<li>Do you warranty your work? — Mention warranty terms.</li>
<li>What payment methods do you accept? — Remove friction.</li>
<li>Can I see examples of your past work? — Link to your portfolio.</li>
<li>How do I schedule service? — Make it easy to book.</li>
</ol>
