<h3>Responding to Negative Reviews</h3>
<p>Every contractor gets a negative review eventually. How you respond matters more than the review itself. 97% of consumers read business responses to reviews, and a professional response to a negative review can actually increase trust.</p>
<p><strong>The negative review response formula:</strong></p>
<div class="code-block">
<pre><code>1. Acknowledge and apologize (even if you disagree)
2. Explain briefly without being defensive
3. Take the conversation offline
4. Offer to make it right
</code></pre>
</div>
<p><strong>Example response:</strong></p>
<blockquote class="highlight-quote">
<p>"[Customer name], we're truly sorry your experience did not meet the standard we hold ourselves to. We take your feedback seriously and have already discussed this with our team. Please call our office at [phone] and ask for [manager name] so we can make this right. We value your business and hope to earn back your trust."</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Rules for negative review responses:</strong><br />
- Respond within 24-48 hours.<br />
- Never argue or blame the customer publicly.<br />
- Never mention specifics that violate privacy (prices, contract details).<br />
- Keep it brief — 3-4 sentences maximum.<br />
- Use the customer's name to show you read their review.</p>
