<h2>Chapter 5: Local Link Building</h2>
<p>Links from other websites to yours remain a powerful ranking signal. For local SEO, the quality and local relevance of links matter more than sheer quantity. A single link from your local Chamber of Commerce can be worth more than 50 links from random directories.</p>
<p>This chapter covers the link building strategies that work specifically for contractors and home service businesses.</p>
<h3>Citation Building</h3>
<p>Citations are mentions of your business name, address, and phone number on other websites. They do not always include a link, but they still signal credibility to Google.</p>
<p><strong>The three tiers of citations:</strong></p>
<div class="cost-table">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Tier</th>
<th>Examples</th>
<th>Priority</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Data aggregators</strong></td>
<td>Data Axle, Neustar Localeze, Foursquare</td>
<td>Submit first — they feed hundreds of directories</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Major directories</strong></td>
<td>Google, Yelp, Bing Places, Apple Maps, Facebook, BBB</td>
<td>Essential for every business</td>
