<h3>Service-Area Specific Errors</h3>
<p>Service-area businesses face unique pitfalls that storefront businesses do not.</p>
<p><strong>Error: Listing as a storefront when you are a service-area business</strong><br />
If customers cannot visit your office, you must hide your address. A visible address on a service-area business is a policy violation that competitors can report.</p>
<p><strong>Error: Using a virtual office or P.O. Box</strong><br />
Google requires a legitimate physical location where you conduct business. Virtual offices and P.O. Boxes will get your profile suspended.</p>
<p><strong>Error: Rapid profile changes</strong><br />
Updating your name, address, phone, and category within a short timeframe triggers Google's spam detection. Make changes gradually and document why each change is necessary.</p>
<h3>Multi-Location Pitfalls</h3>
<p><strong>Error: One GBP for multiple locations</strong><br />
Each physical address needs its own profile. Using one profile for multiple offices violates Google's guidelines.</p>
<p><strong>Error: Duplicate content across location pages</strong><br />
Google penalizes pages with substantially similar content. Every location page needs unique photos, testimonials, and local references.</p>
<p><strong>Error: Linking all GBPs to the homepage</strong><br />
Each location's GBP should link to its dedicated location page, not your homepage. This strengthens the connection between the profile and the relevant geographic content.</p>
<h3>GBP Suspension Risks</h3>
<p>Google suspends Business Profiles for policy violations. A suspended profile disappears from search entirely.</p>
<p><strong>Common suspension triggers:</strong><br />
- Fake or virtual office address<br />
- Keyword-stuffed business name<br />
- Multiple profiles for the same business<br />
- Business type mismatch (e.g., claiming a residential home as a storefront)<br />
- Rapid, suspicious profile changes<br />
- Fake reviews or review manipulation<br />
- Business does not exist at the listed address</p>
<p><strong>If your profile is suspended:</strong><br />
1. Do not create a new profile.<br />
2. Review Google's Business Profile guidelines.<br />
3. Fix the violation.<br />
4. Submit a reinstatement request through Google Business Profile Help.<br />
5. Provide documentation (business license, utility bill, lease agreement).<br />
6. Wait 1-3 weeks for a response.</p>
