<h3>Voice Search Optimization</h3>
<p>Voice search accounts for 20%+ of mobile searches and is growing rapidly. Voice queries are conversational and question-based.</p>
<p><strong>Voice search optimization tactics:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Target question keywords:</strong> "Who is the best plumber in Dallas?" instead of "best plumber Dallas."</li>
<li><strong>Write conversational content:</strong> Use natural language that matches how people speak.</li>
<li><strong>Create FAQ sections:</strong> Voice assistants pull answers from FAQ schema.</li>
<li><strong>Optimize for "near me":</strong> Include "near me" variations naturally in content.</li>
<li><strong>Focus on featured snippets:</strong> Voice assistants often read featured snippet content aloud.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Voice search content framework:</strong></p>
<div class="code-block">
<pre><code>Question: [Exact voice query]
Direct answer: [40-60 word concise answer]
Expanded explanation: [2-3 paragraphs of detail]
Related questions: [3-5 follow-up questions with answers]
</code></pre>
</div>
